WEBVTT

00:47:28.192 --> 00:47:32.016
When we look back on
certain decades -- 1890s, 1880s --

00:47:32.040 --> 00:47:35.898
how many decades do we think the political
leaders were the most important thing

00:47:35.922 --> 00:47:37.087
in that decade?

00:47:37.111 --> 00:47:39.582
In the 1920s? No, it was
the culture, the Flappers.

00:47:39.606 --> 00:47:43.604
In the 1930s, it was the Depression,
but it was also the rise of Hollywood.

00:47:43.628 --> 00:47:46.171
And in the 1950s,
it was, like, James Dean.

00:47:46.195 --> 00:47:47.598
And these figure in today.

00:47:47.622 --> 00:47:50.927
In the 1990s, clearly, it will be
Silicon Valley, maybe even today.

00:47:50.951 --> 00:47:53.607
I often tell young people,
if I were starting my career,

00:47:53.631 --> 00:47:55.993
I'd look into genetics,
I'd look at biogenetics.

00:47:56.017 --> 00:47:58.618
I mean, that's clearly
where the action is going to be.

00:47:58.642 --> 00:48:01.748
But we like to cover things
that have press conferences. (Laughs)